    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27-a2">

                <pb facs="0125" n="23" xml:id="pg23"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex 2]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">List of Persons Suggested to Prime Minister Churchill To
                        See</hi><anchor n="14" xml:id="d27-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#flush">The President Suggests:</p>
                <table rend="width: 90%" rendition="#center">
                    <row>
                        <cell cols="2">Mr. Phillips—who was in India.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d27-f2"
                            />
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Mr. Tobin.</cell>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p rendition="#flush">The Ambassador and Mr. Hopkins Suggest:</p>
                <table rend="width: 99%" rendition="#center">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">The Vice President,<anchor n="16"
                                xml:id="d27-f3"/>
                        </cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Jesse Jones,</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Colonel Stimson,<anchor n="17"
                                xml:id="d27-f4"/>
                        </cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">General Somervell</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Colonel Knox,</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Phil Muray, C.I.O.,</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Morgenthau,</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Bill Green, A.F. of L.,</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Welles,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d27-f5"
                            />
                        </cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mayor Kelly,</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent #top">Mr. Walter Lippmann,</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Spangler, Chairman,<lb/>Republican
                            Party,</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent #top">Mr. Harold Ickes,<anchor n="16"
                                xml:id="d27-f6"/>
                        </cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Frank Walker, Chairman,<lb/>Democratic
                            Party and <lb/> Postmaster General.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Mr. Donald Nelson,</cell>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">General Stilwell,<anchor n="18"
                                xml:id="d27-f7"/>
                        </cell>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">General Chennault,<anchor n="19"
                                xml:id="d27-f8"/>
                        </cell>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">Admiral Land,</cell>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d27-f1" n="14" type="source" xml:id="d27-f1-content">
                <p>It is not known how many of the persons herein listed actually met with
                    Churchill. Available information is set forth in the succeeding footnotes.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f2" n="15" xml:id="d27-f2-content">
                <p>Phillips, who returned from his mission to India at the beginning of May 1943,
                    had an interview with Roosevelt on May 11 and gave the President some additional
                    views in a letter dated May 14, 1943, <ref target="frus1943v04#pg_220">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1943, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, p. 220</ref>. Regarding the meeting
                    between Phillips and Churchill on the
                    morning of May 23, 1943, see the editorial note, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>, <ref target="#pg177">p. 177</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f3" n="16" xml:id="d27-f3-content">
                <p>A participant in the American–British luncheon meeting of May 22, 1943; see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg166">p. 166</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f4" n="17" xml:id="d27-f4-content">
                <p>Stimson participated in the American–British luncheon of May 22, 1943, and met
                    privately with Churchill directly
                    afterwards; see <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg166">pp.
                        166</ref> and <ref target="#pg172">172</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f5" n="16" xml:id="d27-f5-content">
                <p>A participant in the American–British luncheon meeting of May 22, 1943; see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg166">p. 166</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f6" n="16" xml:id="d27-f6-content">
                <p>A participant in the American–British luncheon meeting of May 22, 1943; see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg166">p. 166</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f7" n="18" xml:id="d27-f7-content">
                <p>For Stilwell’s record of his meeting with Churchill on the morning of May 22, 1943, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg165">p. 165</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d27-f8" n="19" xml:id="d27-f8-content">
                <p>According to the account in Claire Lee Chennault, “<hi rendition="#italic">Way of
                        a Fighter</hi> (New York: G. P. Putnam’s Sons, 1949), p. 227, Churchill held a private meeting with
                    Chennault at breakfast sometime near the end of the Conference. No official
                    record of the meeting has been found.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
